  "street_name": "Old Malden Lane",
  "decision_date": "18/11/2025",
  "date_building_work_completed_under_previous_permission": null,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposal constitutes inappropriate development, which by definition is harmful to the Metropolitan Open Land. There are no considerations which when individually or together would clearly outweigh the harm to the Metropolitan Open Land so as to amount to very special circumstances. As such, the development is considered contrary to Paragraph 153 of the National Planning Policy Framework 2024, Policy G3 of the London Plan 2021 and Policy DM5 of the Kingston Core Strategy 2012.",
    "As a matter of fact and degree, the proposed development is not considered to be ancillary to the dwellinghouse known as Wighill. The proposed dwellinghouse is considered to be a separate dwellinghouse which would require full planning permission. Within this context, insufficient information has been submitted to demonstrate the proposal would be exempt from Biodiversity Net Gain, contrary to Paragraph 187 of the National Planning Policy Framework 2024, Policy G6 of the London Plan 2021 and Policy DM6 of the Kingston Core Strategy 2012.",
    "Insufficient information, in terms of a robust Archaeological Assessment, has been submitted to demonstrate the proposed development would not result in harm to archaeological assets within the Tier 2 Archaeological Priority Area (Tolworth Court Farm), contrary to Paragraph 207 of the National Planning Policy Framework 2024, Policy HC1 of the London Plan 2021 and Policy DM12 of the Kingston Core Strategy 2012.",
    "In the absence of a robust Fire Statement being submitted to demonstrate suitable access and equipment for firefighting appliances, or suitable on-site fire suppression systems, it has not been demonstrated that the proposed development would achieve the highest standards of fire safety, contrary to Policy D12(A) of The London Plan (2021).\r"
  ],
